cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below and cite the relevant datasets and methods."
type: software
title: "PET-KLS spatiotemporal brain-map pipeline"
authors:
  - family-names: Monteiro
    given-names: Sara
repository-code: "https://github.com/PET-KLS/Spatiotemporal_microstructure_gradients"
url: "https://github.com/PET-KLS/Spatiotemporal_microstructure_gradients"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Regional modelling of PET-KLS network properties across estimated Alzheimer's
  disease time and spatial comparison with atlas-aligned normative brain maps.
  The downstream regional modelling approach can be adapted to other imaging
  modalities and network metrics.
keywords:
  - neuroimaging
  - PET
  - connectomics
  - generalized additive models
  - spatial analysis
